    "_comment": "Each secondary source's low divided by the primary's, PER SOURCE and never pooled. Pooling was wrong and is why this shape changed (ops#43/ops#44): the rolling-window sources publish only a forward slice, and that slice is measurably cheaper - ScoreBig's covered games had a $33 median low against $48 for the ones it omits, with the date ranges disjoint. A pooled median therefore mixed 'secondary sources ask more' with 'early-season games cost less' and was read as the first. Each source's figure now stands over its own games, with n stated. Sources agreeing on ORDER but differing in LEVEL is the expected shape - they price the same demand with different inventory and fee treatment (all six pairwise Spearman rho 0.98-0.99). A sudden move in one source's ratio means THAT SOURCE changed, not the market."
  },
